\frametitle{Code Snippets: Evaluation}
\small
The validator scores only person IDs observed both at the forecast start and at the future timestamp.
\begin{lstlisting}
shared = sorted(
    set(simulated) & set(actual) & set(initial)
)

social_errors.append(
    math.dist((sx, sy), (truth["x"], truth["y"]))
)
baseline_errors.append(
    math.dist((bx, by), (truth["x"], truth["y"]))
)
\end{lstlisting}
\begin{block}{Fair comparison}
The Social Force forecast and constant-velocity baseline use the same initial observations and matched IDs.
